<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">reinforced-frame</ansi> (blacksmithing recipe)

A light pack-frame of forged strut and pinned joint, welded thin and
tested cruel, stronger for its weight than any honest smith would admit
is possible. Every brace meets its neighbor at an angle that should
buckle and does not. Strap a load to it and the frame carries the weight
somewhere other than your back, though nobody who has built one can
quite explain where.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Crafting ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Skill:</ansi>       blacksmithing (minimum 50)
  <ansi fg="yellow">Station:</ansi>     forge
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ingredients:</ansi> Steel Ingot (x2), Iron Ingot (x1), Coal Dust (x1)

